## Map data

`compositions/mg-hud/data/` carries Natural Earth vector data: the 1:110m land
polygons and the 1:50m coastline clipped to 100–140°E, 15–45°N. Natural Earth
is in the public domain (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/).


## Audio

Not checked in. `scripts/assets.ts` fetches each file and verifies it against
the SHA-256 in `assets/audio/manifest.json`. Every file carries a resolvable
source URL in `assets/audio/ATTRIBUTION.md`, which is the authoritative record
of where each one came from and under what terms.


## Footage and tones

Seven files are tracked under `assets/synthetic/`: three video clips and four
sine tones, produced by ffmpeg from its own `lavfi` sources. No third-party
material is involved, and they are the only moving pictures and the only
sound this repository carries as bytes.

Tracking them is a deliberate exception to the rule that media bytes stay out
of the repository, and the reason is not size: footage is decoded into the pak
at build time, so its bytes are one of the inputs `src/render/identity.ts`
hashes. A digest taken against a clip only one machine has is a digest only
that machine can reproduce.

A command does rebuild them. `assets/synthetic/manifest.json` records the
exact invocation and the first line of `ffmpeg -version` from the run that
produced the committed bytes, beside the SHA-256 `scripts/assets.ts` verifies.
See `assets/synthetic/README.md`.


## The npm package

`scripts/pack.ts` assembles the package from an explicit list, and it
carries less than this repository and more than its tracked source. What it
carries, and under which terms:

  The source in `src/` and the patches in `patches/` — MIT, this file's
  LICENSE.

  Part of the vendored PocketJS tree, prebuilt, at `vendor/pocketjs`: the
  compiler, the framework source, the wasm rasteriser compiled from upstream
  plus `patches/`, and the PNG encoder. MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Yifeng
  "Evan" Wang; the licence travels as `vendor/pocketjs/LICENSE`.

  Upstream's default faces, at `vendor/pocketjs/assets/fonts`: Inter and
  JetBrains Mono, each under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, with
  its text beside it (`LICENSE.txt`, `LICENSE-JetBrainsMono.txt`). They are
  what a composition that declares no `fonts` bakes. Upstream's sample
  images are at `vendor/pocketjs/assets/images`, under its MIT licence.

  The npm packages the compiler imports, at `vendor/pocketjs/node_modules`,
  copied unmodified as `bun install --frozen-lockfile` installed them against
  `vendor/pocketjs/bun.lock`. Each keeps its own licence, and
  `vendor/third-party.json` lists every one with the licence its
  package.json declares and the licence file it ships. The licences among
  them are MIT, ISC, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0 (two packages,
  baseline-browser-mapping and typescript, which the builder loads at
  66caf4e5) and CC-BY-4.0 (one package, caniuse-lite, whose data is
  attributed in its own LICENSE). Three MIT packages publish no
  licence file of their own — @vue-jsx-vapor/compiler-rs, is-reference and
  ts-macro — and travel as npm distributes them.

  The compiler's native binding, @vue-jsx-vapor/compiler-rs-<platform>, is
  not in the package. It is an optional dependency, installed by the
  consumer's package manager from the npm registry under its own MIT licence.

What the package does NOT carry: the HarmonyOS Sans faces, the Noto Sans SC
pair, the Mixkit audio and the synthetic clips and tones — nothing under
this repository's `assets/` — and this repository's compositions, tests,
scripts and ledgers. Nothing in `src/` reads any of them for a composition
outside this repository; a composition's faces and sound are files in its
own project, under whatever terms that project has them.
